      "id": "dlkxytp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Industry"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Industries are classified based on raw materials (agro-based, mineral-based), size (small scale, large scale), and ownership (public, private, joint, cooperative).",
        "India features 8 major industrial clusters, including the Mumbai-Pune, Hugli, Bangalore-Tamil Nadu, and Chota Nagpur regions.",
        "Industrial location depends heavily on geographical factors (raw materials, land, water, power) and non-geographical factors (capital, labor, market, government policies).",
        "The 1991 Industrial Policy dismantled the License Raj, paving the way for Liberalization, Privatization, and Globalization (LPG)."
      ],
      "id": "s5n8ud9"
    },
