    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Chota Nagpur Plateau region is often referred to as the 'Ruhr of India' due to its massive concentration of iron and steel industries.",
        "Understand 'Footloose Industries'—industries like IT and electronics that can be located anywhere as they are not dependent on specific raw materials.",
        "Frequently asked: The Industrial Policy Resolution of 1956 formed the basis of the Second Five-Year Plan focusing on heavy capital goods industries."
      ],
